course: dictionary
lesson: 7282
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word pink is a good example. Usually pink is a light red colour, like many flowers or candyfloss. «"You can't get burnt when it's cloudy," says your big sister, and comes home pink.» Here pink describes skin that has gone a reddish colour from the sun.
explain: Pink can also be a noun: a pink is a small garden flower. «In the pink» is an old-fashioned phrase that means healthy. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. If the sentence is about a garden, pink is a flower. If it is about feeling well, the phrase means healthy.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The alligator snapping turtle lures fish with a pink worm-shaped flap on its tongue.» Put in the colour meaning, and the flap is a pinkish-red colour that looks like a worm. The sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Pink is a light red colour, like many flowers, candyfloss and flamingos.
fact: A pink is a small garden flower, so pink can be a noun as well as an adjective.
fact: «In the pink» means healthy, but it is old-fashioned, so you will hear it less today.
fact: «Tickled pink» means very pleased.
fact: In science, flamingos are pink because of the food they eat.
exercise: «She planted red roses and white pinks in the garden.» What is a pink here? | A healthy feeling | *A small garden flower | A kind of sweet | A light red colour
exercise: «Grandma says she is in the pink after her walk.» What does in the pink mean? | Very tired | Lost | Coloured in paint | *Healthy
exercise: In art class, what colour do you make by mixing red and white paint? | *Pink | Blue | Orange | Black
test: «Tickled pink» means which of these? | *Very pleased | Very cold | Very angry | Very quiet
test: In «a pink worm-shaped flap on its tongue», what does pink describe? | The worm's food | *The flap's colour | The fish's size | The turtle's age
exam: Which sentence uses pink to mean a garden flower? | *«She picked two pinks for the table.» | «The sea glowed pink at sunset.» | «Her cheeks went pink in the cold.» | «The jeans went pale and pink.»
